@slow
Feature: Timesheet security regression checks

  Background:
    Given "curl" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name | value                                  |
      | host | http://localhost:18082/timesheet-devops |

  Scenario: The application answers
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" <host>/
      """
    Then the output should match /^[234][0-9][0-9]$/

  Scenario: Actuator env endpoint is not exposed
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" <host>/actuator/env
      """
    Then the output should not contain "200"

  Scenario: Heapdump is not downloadable
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" <host>/actuator/heapdump
      """
    Then the output should not contain "200"

  Scenario: No stack trace in error responses
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s <host>/this-page-does-not-exist
      """
    Then the output should not contain "at org.springframework"

  Scenario: No X-Powered-By header
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -sI <host>/
      """
    Then the output should not contain "X-Powered-By"

  Scenario: MySQL port is not open on the host
    Given "nmap" is installed
    When I launch an "nmap" attack with:
      """
      nmap -p 3306 localhost
      """
    Then the output should not contain "3306/tcp open"
